QSM Direct source-package preview for Debian contrib
==================================================

Project sponsor: Takt, https://taktcycles.com/
Maintainer: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>

Takt sponsors the project. A Debian Developer able to review and sponsor an
archive upload has not yet been selected. These are different roles.

This is the standalone PVE add-on, not a generic Debian desktop service.
pve-manager, qemu-server and optional pve-container are external runtime
dependencies; all compilation dependencies come from Debian main. No
proprietary GPU driver is required to compile or use software encoding.

The monorepository also contains historic experiments, patch submissions,
lab captures and release evidence. The upstream source export intentionally
contains the standalone source, build/test inputs and packaging only. The
export helper records its git revision and hashes. It excludes downloaded
packages, prebuilt binaries, benchmark captures, native Proxmox patch series
and optional patched Sway/SDDM source builds. Those optional compositor
experiments are not bundled into this Debian source package.

Build with dpkg-buildpackage or sbuild after installing Build-Depends. The
source root is qsm-direct, not the QEMU monorepository root. The worker is
compiled by CMake with dpkg hardening flags; no network access is used by
the build. LXC's embedded guest deb is built from this same source during
the binary-indep sequence, never downloaded or taken from a release asset.

The source and packaging use AI assistance. Before any Debian upload they
need human review for correctness, maintenance and licensing. Public test
evidence does not assert that a Debian Developer has performed that review.

The .dsc/.changes signatures on an external review release, if present,
identify the project release key; they do not imply a Debian upload or an
individual Debian Developer identity. The current signed stock3 APT feed
is separate and is not switched to this packaging preview automatically.
